				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mist): Advance Documentation/Rust submodule pointer\n\nUpdate the Documentation/Rust submodule from `fd168457` to `f50a4c0f`, picking up the latest Rust documentation commits for the Mist component.\n\nThis non-functional update keeps the checked-out documentation in sync with the repository's latest revisions.",
			"SHA": "df5bce044c4c618d41eca053e7b105e5243ef8e1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-30T19:12:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				8
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mist): Reconcile domain references with active land.playform.cloud\n\nUpdate the Mist DNS isolation server to use land.playform.cloud as the authoritative zone across source files and documentation, replacing residual editor.land references from the grace-hold period.\n\nSource changes in ForwardSecurity.rs, Library.rs, Resolver.rs, Server.rs, and Zone.rs standardize zone origins, forward allowlists, and domain matching logic on land.playform.cloud. Resolver.rs drops the editor.land predicate for LandDnsResolver; Zone.rs regenerates SOA, NS, and wildcard A records under land.playform.cloud; ForwardSecurity.rs switches the forward allowlist from update.editor.land to update.land.playform.cloud.\n\nDocumentation changes in Architecture.md, DeepDive.md, and README.md realign module tables, Mermaid architecture diagrams, sequence flows, and DNS zone record samples. DeepDive.md adds a preface clarifying that editor.land is the former domain while land.playform.cloud is the current production runtime target.",
			"SHA": "561c262e4390693caaa8803a7f06e6ba0d2a6bb5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T19:04:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				5
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Remove `Air` from DNS resolver consumers\n\nUpdate the Mist component documentation to reflect that `Air` no longer directly consumes the Mist DNS resolver. The `Air` sidecar's previous role of configuring its `reqwest` HTTP client with the local resolver has been removed.\n\nThe network isolation provided by Mist now covers `Cocoon` and `Air` via explicit allowlisting, but `Air` is no longer listed as a direct consumer of the `LandDnsResolver` implementation. Update diagrams and descriptions in `Architecture.md` and `DeepDive.md` to remove `Air` from the consumer graph and startup sequence.\n\nAlso add blank lines in `ForwardSecurity.rs`, `Resolver.rs`, and `WebSocket.rs` to improve readability around control flow blocks, adhering to Rust style conventions.",
			"SHA": "7d6f3751dd43d90b796be0186a6dce36ab71ef0a"
		}
	],
